---
layout: base.njk
description: "Give it your website. Prospektor finds the companies worth approaching, names who to write to, and writes the pitch in your voice."
# One page per language the build knows (#114): `/` in English, `/es/` and so
# on for every catalogue under src/_data/strings/. Every sentence below sits
# in a {% t %} block and renders untouched on the English page; the pagination
# is what makes the other languages exist at all. Nothing here lists them.
pagination:
  data: languages
  size: 1
  alias: language
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "{{ language.prefix }}/"
---

{#- The homepage in the studio's look (#1092, 7 Oct 2026): the grey ground,
    white cards with no border and no shadow, and coral on exactly one press,
    the scan field's. The words are the studio's own names for its screens
    (Leads for you, Research, Counterprospekt, a glance, Decision-makers, Warm
    intros, Library, Inbound), because a visitor who signs up should meet the
    menu they read about. The five agents, the six-stage run card and the
    batch band are gone with the run model they described.

    The operator on the draft: "keep it minimal and clean. I want the primary
    CTA still to be clearly to scan the site and not immediately go into
    product screenshots." So the hero is the promise, one sentence, the field
    and one quiet line to the demo, and nothing else.

    #207: the anchor is the SECTION, not the field inside it. Every "Scan your
    site" on this site is a /#scan jump; the hero is the first thing in the
    document, so the target resolves to scroll 0 and the headline and the
    field arrive together. test/drive.js §6b measures it. -#}
<section class="hero" id="scan">
  {#- .hero-rest collapses when a scan starts (scan.js adds .scan-focus to
      the hero): from that moment the scan is the page. -#}
  <div class="hero-rest" id="heroRest">
    {#- #453: the h1 carries the words the <title> shows (site.tagline), and
        test/pages.test.js holds the two together. -#}
    <h1>{% t %}Leads that fit you, and what to send them{% endt %}</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">{% t %}Give it your website. It finds the companies worth approaching and writes the pitch in your voice.{% endt %}</p>
  </div>

  <!-- The scan field: POST /api/scan, poll, render the proposal. scan.js drives it. -->
  <div class="scan-hero">
    <form class="scan-form" id="scanForm" novalidate>
      <div class="scan-q">
        <svg class="scan-q-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle><path d="M20 20l-3.5-3.5"></path></svg>
        {#- #241: the field is a combobox over #scanSuggest; the browser's own
            URL autofill is off so it cannot draw a second list over ours. -#}
        <input class="scan-input" id="scanInput" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="off"
               role="combobox" aria-autocomplete="list" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="scanSuggest"
               spellcheck="false" placeholder="yourcompany.com" aria-label="{% t %}Your company website{% endt %}">
      </div>
      <button class="scan-btn" type="submit" id="scanBtn">{% t %}Find my leads{% endt %}</button>
      {#- #241: companies matching what has been typed, one line each (name,
          domain), written by scan.js from the site's own company-suggest
          function. Picking one fills the field; nothing else moves. -#}
      <ul class="scan-suggest" id="scanSuggest" role="listbox" hidden></ul>
    </form>
    {#- The hint and the demo's door (#767) read as one line under the field.
        The door is a link and never a second button (style rule 8), and it
        goes with the rest of the hero the moment a scan starts. -#}
    <div class="scan-hints">
      <p class="scan-hint" id="scanHint">{% t %}Free, no sign-up, about 30 seconds.{% endt %}</p>
      <p class="scan-demo" id="scanDemo"><a href="{{ '/demo/' | localize }}">{% t %}Or click through the demo.{% endt %}</a></p>
    </div>
    <p class="scan-error" id="scanError" hidden></p>

    <div aria-live="polite">
      <div class="scan-status" id="scanStatus" hidden>
        <div class="scan-progress"><div class="scan-progress-fill" id="scanBarFill"></div></div>
        <div class="scan-status-line"><span class="building-dot"></span><span id="scanStatusMsg"></span></div>
      </div>

      {#- #240: one card, the exact width of the search bar above it. Name +
          domain, fact chips, the proposal: that's the whole result. -#}
      <div class="scan-result" id="scanResult" hidden>
        <div class="scan-card">
          <div class="scan-card-head">
            <span class="scan-card-name" id="scanName"></span>
            <span class="scan-card-domain" id="scanDomain"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="scan-chips" id="scanFacts" hidden></div>
          <p class="scan-lead">{% t %}Here's what Prospektor will find for you:{% endt %}</p>
          {#- Not a heading (#137): written by scan.js after the fetch returns. -#}
          <p class="scan-guess" id="scanGuess" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
          {#- #419: the free run is the primary action here, not checkout. The
              way to pay stays on the card as one quiet line, demoted and never
              removed, because the reader who is already sold must not have to
              hunt for it. -#}
          <div class="scan-cta-row">
            <a class="btn-cta" id="scanRunCta" href="https://studio.prospektor.ai/r">{% t %}Show me the companies →{% endt %}</a>
            <p class="scan-cta-note">{% t %}Free, no sign-up.{% endt %} <a id="scanCta" data-signup href="{{ site.studio }}/signup{% if language.code != 'en' %}?lang={{ language.code }}{% endif %}">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="scan-fallback" id="scanFallback" hidden>
        <p class="scan-fallback-msg" id="scanFallbackMsg" hidden></p>
        <a class="btn-cta" id="scanFallbackCta" data-signup href="{{ site.studio }}/signup{% if language.code != 'en' %}?lang={{ language.code }}{% endif %}">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/scan.js' | asset }}" defer></script>

{#- The studio's menu, as it is: four questions, in the order you ask them
    about a company. Keeps id="what" so old deep links land. -#}
<section class="sec" id="what">
  <div class="col">
    <h2>{% t %}Every screen answers one question{% endt %}</h2>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="hcard">
        <p class="hcard-q">{% t %}Who?{% endt %}</p>
        <div class="hrow"><span class="tile" aria-hidden="true">L</span><div><b>{% t %}Leads for you{% endt %}</b><span>{% t %}Companies worth approaching this week, each with the reason it fits.{% endt %}</span></div></div>
        <div class="hrow"><span class="tile" aria-hidden="true">R</span><div><b>{% t %}Research{% endt %}</b><span>{% t %}Read one company, find more like it, or hand it a whole list.{% endt %}</span></div></div>
        <div class="hrow"><span class="tile" aria-hidden="true">C</span><div><b>Counterprospekt</b><span>{% t %}Who buys from your competitors. Their clients are your next leads.{% endt %}</span></div></div>
        <p class="hcard-foot"><a href="{{ '/who-to-pitch/' | localize }}">{% t %}See who to pitch{% endt %} ›</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hcard">
        <p class="hcard-q">{% t %}What to say?{% endt %}</p>
        <div class="hrow"><span class="tile" aria-hidden="true">P</span><div><b>{% t %}The pitch{% endt %}</b><span>{% t %}Deck, one-pager, cold email and proposal, in your voice and grounded in what has worked for you.{% endt %}</span></div></div>
        <div class="hrow"><span class="tile" aria-hidden="true">I</span><div><b>{% t %}Inbound{% endt %}</b><span>{% t %}Answer a lead who wrote to you, or prepare the call.{% endt %}</span></div></div>
        <div class="hrow"><span class="tile" aria-hidden="true">B</span><div><b>{% t %}Library{% endt %}</b><span>{% t %}Every pitch you have written, ready to share or push to your CRM.{% endt %}</span></div></div>
        <p class="hcard-foot"><a href="{{ '/what-to-send/' | localize }}">{% t %}See what to send{% endt %} ›</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hcard">
        <p class="hcard-q">{% t %}Who at them?{% endt %}</p>
        <div class="hrow"><span class="tile" aria-hidden="true">D</span><div><b>{% t %}Decision-makers{% endt %}</b><span>{% t %}The people to write to, with their emails and where each was found.{% endt %}</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hcard">
        <p class="hcard-q">{% t %}Who can walk you in?{% endt %}</p>
        <div class="hrow"><span class="tile" aria-hidden="true">W</span><div><b>{% t %}Warm intros{% endt %}</b><span>{% t %}Who you already know who can introduce you, and the note to send them.{% endt %}</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- A glance, shown rather than described. The example is the studio's own
    (Ledgerpost pitching Harborline Freight, the seller the demo signs in as),
    and the card says it is invented. One worked example and no scale: the
    method is published, never the mechanics (#746). Keeps id="how". -#}
<section class="sec" id="how">
  <div class="col glance">
    <div class="glance-say">
      <h2>{% t %}A glance before you pitch{% endt %}</h2>
      <p class="lede">{% t %}Fifteen seconds tells you whether a company is worth a full pitch: a fit score, the one argument, and what counts against it.{% endt %}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hcard glance-card">
      <div class="gco">
        <span class="glogo" aria-hidden="true">H</span>
        <div><div class="gname">Harborline Freight</div><div class="gmeta">{% t %}Freight forwarding · 380 staff{% endt %}</div></div>
        <div class="gscore"><b>94</b><small>{% t %}fit{% endt %}</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gmeter" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
      <p class="gone">{% t %}Harborline rekeys every customs filing by hand, and Ledgerpost already holds the data being rekeyed.{% endt %}</p>
      <ul class="gsig">
        <li>{% t %}240,000 shipments a year through 14 ports.{% endt %}</li>
        <li>{% t %}Nine operations staff rekey customs filings full time.{% endt %}</li>
        <li class="against">{% t %}Signed a three-year TMS contract in March.{% endt %}</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="gwho"><span>{% t %}Write to the Head of Customs and the COO{% endt %}</span><span class="ghost">{% t %}Write the pitch{% endt %}</span></div>
      <p class="gex">{% t %}Harborline and Ledgerpost are invented for this example.{% endt %}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The thesis, priced. Keeps id="pricing": Stripe's cancel_url is /#pricing
    (test/checkout-session.test.js) and old deep links land here. #1097: the
    paid card's link opens the studio's sign-up, finished by signup.js. -#}
<section class="sec" id="pricing">
  <div class="col">
    <h2>{% t %}Who to pitch is free. What to send is paid.{% endt %}</h2>
    <p class="lede">{% t %}One workspace, one price, your whole team in.{% endt %}</p>
    <div class="grid2 price">
      <div class="hcard">
        <p class="hcard-q">{% t %}Who to pitch{% endt %}</p>
        <b class="big">{% t %}Free{% endt %}</b>
        <p class="per">{% t %}No card, no sign-up to start{% endt %}</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>{% t %}Your site read, and what you should hunt for{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Three companies that fit, scored{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Who buys from one of your competitors{% endt %}</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="hcard-foot"><a href="#scan">{% t %}Scan your site{% endt %} ›</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hcard">
        <p class="hcard-q">{% t %}What to send{% endt %}</p>
        <b class="big">{% t %}$999 a month{% endt %}</b>
        <p class="per">{% t %}or $9,990 a year, two months free{% endt %}</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>{% t %}Every pitch: deck, one-pager, cold email, proposal{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Warm intros from your network{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Replies to inbound, and a sheet for every call{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Your whole team, no seats to count{% endt %}</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="hcard-foot buy" id="buy"><a href="{{ site.studio }}/signup{% if language.code != 'en' %}?lang={{ language.code }}{% endif %}" id="buyLink" data-signup>{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a> <a class="quiet" href="{{ '/pricing/' | localize }}">{% t %}See pricing{% endt %} ›</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/signup.js' | asset }}" defer></script>

{#- #830/#838: the directory has a page per integration; the chips are its
    doors. Logos are the directory's own files (#841). -#}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="col">
    <h2>{% t %}Works where you already work{% endt %}</h2>
    <p class="lede">{% t %}Your own Claude or ChatGPT can run Prospektor, and a finished pitch goes to your CRM in one press.{% endt %}</p>
    <div class="chips">
      {%- for c in [['claude', 'Claude'], ['chatgpt', 'ChatGPT'], ['hubspot', 'HubSpot'], ['attio', 'Attio'], ['close', 'Close'], ['affinity', 'Affinity'], ['slack', 'Slack']] %}
      <a class="chip" href="{{ ('/integrations/' + c[0] + '/') | localize }}"><img src="{{ ('/assets/img/integrations/' + c[0] + '.svg') | asset }}" alt="" width="18" height="18">{{ c[1] }}</a>
      {%- endfor %}
      <a class="chip" href="{{ '/integrations/' | localize }}">{% t %}All integrations{% endt %} ›</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
